      <memberdef kind="function" id="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_io_uring_batched_sender_1a8382401ddeeaca2aaba1b094d9f848f7" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool themis::network::IoUringBatchedSender::enqueue</definition>
        <argsstring>(WireProtocolBatcher &amp;batcher)</argsstring>
        <name>enqueue</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::network::IoUringBatchedSender::enqueue</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_wire_protocol_batcher" kindref="compound">WireProtocolBatcher</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>batcher</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Queue all pending iov entries of <computeroutput>batcher</computeroutput> for the next send round. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Enqueue.</para>
<para>If io_uring is unavailable the pending data is written immediately via <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_wire_protocol_batcher_1a31f5e18021f06b3c100c57156add0259" kindref="member">WireProtocolBatcher::flush()</ref></computeroutput> and the return value mirrors that call.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>batcher</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A batcher with pending data (<computeroutput>batcher.pending() == true</computeroutput>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>true on success; false if the SQ ring is full or flush failed.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">batcher</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input/output parameter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True when the operation succeeds.</para>
</simplesect>
Calls: pending(), defined(), flush(). </para>
