        <type>size_t</type>
        <definition>size_t themis::network::IoUringBatchedSender::submitAndWait</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>submitAndWait</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::network::IoUringBatchedSender::submitAndWait</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Submit all queued SQEs and wait for all CQEs to complete. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Submit And Wait.</para>
<para>Blocks until every previously enqueued operation has been acknowledged by the kernel. This is the only syscall issued for the whole batch.</para>
<para>No-op (returns immediately) when io_uring is unavailable — all sends have already been executed synchronously inside <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_io_uring_batched_sender_1a8382401ddeeaca2aaba1b094d9f848f7" kindref="member">enqueue()</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Number of bytes successfully written across all operations. Individual operation errors are counted in <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_io_uring_batched_sender_1a084d198c16b2eb474868dd1117c32cd8" kindref="member">lastStats()</ref>.errors</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Return value.</para>
</simplesect>
Calls: defined(), empty(), size(), enqueueSqe(), data(), io_uring_enter(), THEMIS_ERROR(), std::strerror(). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
