    <briefdescription>
<para>Batched sender that amortises syscall overhead across connections. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Usage: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_io_uring_batched_sender_1ae8576382db9728d971154e108a871e4a" kindref="member">IoUringBatchedSender</ref><sp/>sender(256);<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>queue_depth</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(!sender.isAvailable())<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>fall<sp/>back<sp/>to<sp/>individual<sp/>WireProtocolBatcher::flush()<sp/>calls</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">for</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>batcher<sp/>:<sp/>active_batchers)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>sender.enqueue(batcher);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">sender.submitAndWait();<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>one<sp/>io_uring_enter()<sp/>for<sp/>all</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>stats<sp/>=<sp/>sender.lastStats();<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>inspect<sp/>results</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>When io_uring is not available <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_io_uring_batched_sender_1ac55e58cac7cab63c357579015a4d5a9c" kindref="member">isAvailable()</ref></computeroutput> returns false and <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_io_uring_batched_sender_1a8382401ddeeaca2aaba1b094d9f848f7" kindref="member">enqueue()</ref></computeroutput> immediately calls <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_wire_protocol_batcher_1a31f5e18021f06b3c100c57156add0259" kindref="member">WireProtocolBatcher::flush()</ref></computeroutput> so the caller&apos;s loop body stays identical in both paths. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
